Glassket-Orbital

Ingredients: POST-ROCK + CELESTIAL, SPACE & ORBITAL + Marimba  
Creative Catalyst: The style was codified by grandmothers who DJ at a floating market before dawn.

A shimmering, seismic collision where the woody, resonant clack of ancient percussion collides with towering, zero-gravity guitar crescendos. Glassket-Orbital mimics the physical physics of low-Earth orbit as witnessed through morning mist: hyper-reverberant rosewood marimbas loop through delay pedals powered by wet boat batteries, punctuated by long, tectonic sheets of feedback that swell like solar flares hitting the upper atmosphere. It sounds like a cathedral made of spun sugar and molten lead collapsing in slow motion into a tidal river.

Genre DNA
- Tempo & Pulse: 45–72 BPM; polyrhythmic, rubato-heavy waltz metrics (9/8 overlapping 4/4) that drift like unanchored sampans before locking into massive, slow-motion engine-thrum downbeats.
- Harmonic Palette: Lydian Dominant and suspended pentatonic scales, microtonally detuned by ambient temperature shifts to create shimmering, iridescent beat-frequencies.
- Production Signatures: 
  1. Sub-Hydrophonic Resonant Tracking: Mic’ing marimba bars underwater using modified hydrophones to catch lower-end fluid decay.
  2. Orbital Tail Siphon: Routing guitars through infinite-decay space-echo units modulated by real-time shortwave radio atmospheric static.
  3. Grandmother’s Compression: Over-saturating master buses through valve-driven tape decks originally built for maritime navigation broadcasts.
- Dynamics: Glacial, multi-minute swells starting from whisper-quiet, skeletal wood-strikes that gradually build into crushing, planetary walls of distortion, only to dissolve back into cosmic vacuum.

